# Host-side scanner replay

Once a Samsung fixture is in `.scan-fixtures/replay/`, **do not** ask the user to
tap Scanner Lab / Run live pipeline / upload for recognition-logic changes.

Evaluate with:

- `yarn scan:replay <fixture-id>` — one fixture (recorded OCR + portable warp)
- `yarn scan:regression` — full corpus gate

Those cover CardNameIndex, fuzzy match, variant consensus, title decode, and
acceptance. Recorded strings such as `Maddenino Hey` / `Maddening Hesy` are the
Samsung OCR observations.

## HOST REPLAYABLE (Mac / Cursor)

Warp, title crop, preprocess, CardNameIndex, strong-fuzzy, fusion/acceptance
from recorded OCR or existing pixels.

## DEVICE REQUIRED

New camera captures, native detector, focus/camera, or a **fresh** Android ML Kit
reading. Only then: inbox upload, or `yarn scan:device-replay <fixture-id>` if
the phone worker is on.

Do not pretend Node reproduces ML Kit. Do not duplicate the same PNG into the
corpus twice.
